1
00:00:00,280 --> 00:00:01,400
Look at this letter.

2
00:00:02,360 --> 00:00:02,640
C.

3
00:00:03,880 --> 00:00:06,050
C has two different sounds.

4
00:00:06,820 --> 00:00:07,960
Listen to the first one.

5
00:00:09,240 --> 00:00:09,360
Cat.

6
00:00:10,500 --> 00:00:12,250
The c says /k/.

7
00:00:14,080 --> 00:00:15,460
Now listen to the second one.

8
00:00:16,800 --> 00:00:17,280
City.

9
00:00:18,400 --> 00:00:19,500
The c says /s/.

10
00:00:22,180 --> 00:00:26,100
It is the same letter, but it makes two different sounds!

11
00:00:27,200 --> 00:00:29,560
So how do we know which sound to say?

12
00:00:30,660 --> 00:00:33,780
In our last videos, we looked at the letter before.

13
00:00:35,100 --> 00:00:37,240
This time, we look the other way.

14
00:00:38,020 --> 00:00:40,680
We look at the letter that comes after the c.

15
00:00:42,260 --> 00:00:43,080
Here is the rule!

16
00:00:44,240 --> 00:00:45,660
Three letters are special.

17
00:00:46,860 --> 00:00:47,200
E.

18
00:00:47,900 --> 00:00:48,620
I.

19
00:00:49,300 --> 00:00:50,000
Y.

20
00:00:51,340 --> 00:00:57,520
When c sees e, i or y coming next, the c goes soft.

21
00:00:59,120 --> 00:01:04,220
A soft c says /s/, like a quiet little snake.

22
00:01:04,740 --> 00:01:05,180
Listen.

23
00:01:06,000 --> 00:01:07,300
/s/...

24
00:01:07,400 --> 00:01:07,520
ih...

25
00:01:08,200 --> 00:01:08,660
ty...

26
00:01:10,000 --> 00:01:10,840
City!

27
00:01:12,120 --> 00:01:16,440
The i comes right after the c, so this c is soft.

28
00:01:18,120 --> 00:01:19,920
Here are more soft c words.

29
00:01:21,080 --> 00:01:21,340
Cent.

30
00:01:22,440 --> 00:01:23,400
Circle.

31
00:01:24,560 --> 00:01:25,320
Cycle.

32
00:01:26,680 --> 00:01:32,280
Every one of them has e, i or y right after the c.

33
00:01:33,700 --> 00:01:35,300
So what happens everywhere else?

34
00:01:36,960 --> 00:01:40,110
Everywhere else, the c stays hard.

35
00:01:40,800 --> 00:01:44,840
A hard c says /k/, strong and short.

36
00:01:46,000 --> 00:01:46,320
Listen.

37
00:01:47,560 --> 00:01:48,660
/k/...

38
00:01:48,720 --> 00:01:48,820
a...

39
00:01:49,560 --> 00:01:50,640
t...

40
00:01:50,720 --> 00:01:51,400
Cat!

41
00:01:52,560 --> 00:01:57,800
The a comes after the c, and a is not one of our three letters.

42
00:01:58,640 --> 00:02:00,470
So this c stays hard.

43
00:02:02,140 --> 00:02:03,860
Here are more hard c words.

44
00:02:05,140 --> 00:02:05,540
Cup.

45
00:02:06,660 --> 00:02:07,280
Cold.

46
00:02:08,940 --> 00:02:09,080
Clap.

47
00:02:10,840 --> 00:02:14,060
In clap, the letter l comes after the c.

48
00:02:14,980 --> 00:02:15,500
That is fine.

49
00:02:16,320 --> 00:02:18,020
The c is still hard.

50
00:02:19,800 --> 00:02:22,900
Let's say our three special letters one more time.

51
00:02:24,020 --> 00:02:24,460
E.

52
00:02:24,940 --> 00:02:25,920
I.

53
00:02:26,720 --> 00:02:27,400
Y.

54
00:02:28,600 --> 00:02:30,720
Those three make the c soft.

55
00:02:32,420 --> 00:02:34,440
Every other letter keeps it hard.

56
00:02:35,660 --> 00:02:38,080
Now let's look at more soft c words.

57
00:02:39,520 --> 00:02:39,800
City.

58
00:02:41,200 --> 00:02:41,480
Cent.

59
00:02:43,060 --> 00:02:43,600
Circle.

60
00:02:45,020 --> 00:02:45,640
Cycle.

61
00:02:47,100 --> 00:02:47,380
Ice.

62
00:02:49,200 --> 00:02:49,460
Race.

63
00:02:50,880 --> 00:02:55,440
Every one has e, i or y after the c.

64
00:02:56,800 --> 00:02:59,120
Now let's look at the hard c words.

65
00:03:00,360 --> 00:03:00,520
Cat.

66
00:03:01,820 --> 00:03:02,320
Cup.

67
00:03:03,620 --> 00:03:04,360
Cold.

68
00:03:05,800 --> 00:03:06,320
Clap.

69
00:03:07,900 --> 00:03:08,240
Cream.

70
00:03:09,620 --> 00:03:10,120
Picnic.

71
00:03:11,160 --> 00:03:15,900
Not one of them has e, i or y after the c.

72
00:03:17,220 --> 00:03:18,980
You're doing really well!

73
00:03:19,900 --> 00:03:23,820
If you're enjoying this, please like this video and subscribe.

74
00:03:24,660 --> 00:03:27,480
Then we can keep making more videos for you.

75
00:03:29,080 --> 00:03:30,860
There is one more thing you should know.

76
00:03:32,140 --> 00:03:33,580
Look at these five words.

77
00:03:35,220 --> 00:03:35,420
Special.

78
00:03:36,780 --> 00:03:37,200
Precious.

79
00:03:38,900 --> 00:03:39,540
Musician.

80
00:03:40,880 --> 00:03:41,420
Ancient.

81
00:03:42,860 --> 00:03:43,580
Ocean.

82
00:03:44,760 --> 00:03:47,080
Every one of them has a soft c.

83
00:03:48,220 --> 00:03:49,280
But listen carefully.

84
00:03:50,420 --> 00:03:52,580
This soft c does not say /s/.

85
00:03:54,060 --> 00:03:55,330
It says /sh/.

86
00:03:57,080 --> 00:03:59,330
Can you see what makes these words special?

87
00:04:00,860 --> 00:04:02,640
Look at how each one ends.

88
00:04:03,080 --> 00:04:05,840
/shəl/.

89
00:04:05,840 --> 00:04:06,040
/shəs/.

90
00:04:07,520 --> 00:04:08,160
/shən/.

91
00:04:09,140 --> 00:04:10,020
/shənt/.

92
00:04:11,520 --> 00:04:12,180
/shən/.

93
00:04:13,940 --> 00:04:18,430
When the c is followed by two vowels like that, it says /sh/.

94
00:04:20,180 --> 00:04:23,440
That is a rule of its own, and it has its own video.

95
00:04:24,040 --> 00:04:25,640
So don't worry about it today.

96
00:04:26,520 --> 00:04:28,210
Just remember the big thing.

97
00:04:29,040 --> 00:04:34,400
Before e, i or y, the c is always soft.

98
00:04:35,400 --> 00:04:37,230
It is never, ever hard.

99
00:04:39,120 --> 00:04:40,150
Now it's your turn!

100
00:04:41,000 --> 00:04:41,930
Here is the word...

101
00:04:42,800 --> 00:04:43,360
Cycle.

102
00:04:44,280 --> 00:04:45,660
Is this c hard...

103
00:04:46,560 --> 00:04:47,360
or is it soft?

104
00:04:49,480 --> 00:04:51,400
It is soft!

105
00:04:51,400 --> 00:04:53,840
The y comes right after the c.

106
00:04:54,960 --> 00:04:56,260
Let's remember it together.

107
00:04:57,220 --> 00:05:02,460
Before e, i or y, the c is soft.

108
00:05:03,640 --> 00:05:05,820
A soft c usually says /s/.

109
00:05:07,600 --> 00:05:11,100
Everywhere else, the c is hard and says /k/.

110
00:05:13,480 --> 00:05:15,010
Want to hear these sounds again?

111
00:05:15,960 --> 00:05:18,540
They are all waiting in the English Learning app.

112
00:05:19,360 --> 00:05:20,880
It costs nothing at all!
